6. Control Unit (CU)
The Control Unit (CU) is responsible for coordinating all CPU operations.

- It generates control signals based on:
  - Decoded instruction information
  - Timing signals from the sequence counter
  - System status flags
- The control unit sequences the CPU through the fetch, decode, execute, and interrupt phases.
- It ensures that registers, ALU, memory, and bus operations occur in the correct order and at the correct time.

The control unit acts as the “brain” of the Pulse-12 CPU, ensuring correct and orderly instruction execution.
